==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|Norfolk}}, {{l|en|territory|Territory}} {{l|en|of}} Norfolk Island

===Etymology===
From the [[duchy]] of {{m|en|Norfolk}} in [[England]], q.v. As an Ecuadorian island, clipping of [[Duke of Norfolk's Island]], bestowed by {{w|William Ambrosia Cowley}} in 1684 honor of {{w|Henry Howard, 6th Duke of Norfolk}}; his son {{w|Henry Howard, 7th Duke of Norfolk|Henry, the 7th duke}}; or both. As an Australian island and territory, bestowed by {{w|James Cook}} in 1774 in honor of {{w|Mary Howard, Duchess of Norfolk|Mary Howard}}, wife of the {{w|Edward Howard, 9th Duke of Norfolk|9th duke}}.

